# Kasimir Velikov walks his road (docs/voice/kasimir_velikov.md; Story Allies Presence Plan, package K1). In five parts:
#   camp_*: the camp conversation's opening line once the party has come back from the Amber Temple with news of Patrina,
#       or Kasimir has made his peace or lost his warmth (vallaki/kasimir:start jumps here, and each node goes on to that
#       file's menu).
#   come: "Come with us to the temple" from the camp's menu (his scenes there then play as they do for the Tarokka's
#       Seer, amber_temple/patrina:kasimir_meets and vestiges:tarakamedes_kasimir). Not for the Seer's own ally.
#   rest_told, destroyed_told: the two closures he can only get at the camp, when the party dealt with Patrina without
#       him. (A bargain at Tarakamedes is the temple's own scene; where he goes after it is package K2.)
#   homeward: walking with the party once Patrina is at rest (patrina_fate == rest), he offers to go home unless they
#       ask him to stay. Not asked of the Seer's ally, who sees the end through (StoryState.guest_stays), nor after the
#       bargain.
#   talk: his hub, opened from the camp's menu and, while he travels, by clicking him (guest_talk in
#       data/npcs/kasimir_velikov.json). The menu holds the three newest topics not yet heard (hub_menu), each of
#       which plays once: the Vallaki news the Vistani bring to their fire (only at the camp), the Tome's page on the
#       dusk elves, what a dark gift costs, and warnings about Tarakamedes and Vosk read from the temple's own flags.
# Side flags live in data/flags/allies_kasimir.json. Lines were drafted by Gemini through the ai-bridge
# (docs/plans/gemini_allies/K1/) and edited. All unvoiced.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The camp's opening lines

~ camp_news_rest
Kasimir: You still carry the mountain air on your cloaks. Sit by the wagon, please, and tell me plainly.
-> vallaki/kasimir:menu

~ camp_news_destroyed
Kasimir [sad]: You have been up into the ice, and you do not look at me. Say what you have come to say.
-> vallaki/kasimir:menu

~ camp_peace
Kasimir [smile]: Welcome back. The wagon is only the second saddest place in the camp now, which is a strange comfort.
-> vallaki/kasimir:menu

~ camp_cold
Kasimir: You have returned. Tell me what you require, and we will conclude our business.
-> vallaki/kasimir:menu

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Come with us to the temple

~ come
Narrator: He folds the half-mended net into a neat square and sets it on the stool, though his fingers linger on the cord.
Kasimir: You are kind to remember my errand.
Kasimir [smile]: I warn you that three centuries beside a wagon have made me very dull company on a road.
Kasimir [weary]: The pass is cold, and what waits in the amber is colder still.
Kasimir: I ask only one courtesy: when we find my sister, let me be the first to speak to her.
# The road into the mountains is his now, so is the Beggar's treasure (as in vallaki/kasimir:ally and :trade).
if treasure_at:vallaki_vistani_camp:camp_edge
Kasimir: And you will want this. I was keeping it for whoever would take me into the mountains. It seems that is you.
reading give vallaki_vistani_camp:camp_edge
endif
join kasimir_velikov
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Laid to rest without him

~ rest_told
Kasimir: I have waited a very long time to hear her name spoken by someone who has seen her.
Kasimir [sad]: Tell me what she said to you, if she could speak at all.
* She asked us to tell you she is done waiting. -> rest_waiting
* Not yet. We cannot speak of it like this. -> rest_later

~ rest_later
Kasimir [sad]: I have waited three hundred years for that word, so I can wait a little longer. Come to my fire when you are ready.
-> vallaki/kasimir:menu

~ rest_waiting
Kasimir [sad]: Three hundred years in the cold, and I kept her there with my own cowardice.
Kasimir: It is like her to lose patience with me at the end. Was there more?
* She said the stones hurt less than the quiet afterward. -> rest_quiet
* That is all she said to us. -> rest_close

~ rest_quiet
Kasimir [sad]: I stood in the back and made no sound while the stones fell. Afterward, none of us spoke her name.
Kasimir [weary]: We thought silence was survival, when it was only another grave. Did she say anything else?
* She said you were always very good at quiet. -> rest_good
* That is all she said to us. -> rest_close

~ rest_good
Kasimir [smile]: Even as a spirit in the ice, she keeps her edge.
Kasimir [sad]: Yes, I was very good at quiet. I think I am finished practicing it now.
-> rest_close

~ rest_close
set kasimir_heard_rest
Narrator: He lets the net slide from his lap to the ground, and his hands, for once, do not go after it. The lake wind stirs his coat, smelling of cold water and wet ash.
Kasimir: Thank you for climbing where I was too afraid to go, and for bringing her words down the mountain.
Kasimir [weary]: I will sit here a little longer and listen to the water, with nothing in my hands.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Destroyed

~ destroyed_told
Kasimir [sad]: You need not tell me how it ended, or whose hand struck the blow.
Kasimir [sad]: Tell me only one thing, if you will: was she afraid?
* No. She was angry, and she was herself. -> destroyed_no
* Yes. She was afraid at the end. -> destroyed_yes
* We cannot say. We are very sorry. -> destroyed_unknown

~ destroyed_no
Kasimir [sad]: Proud to the last, then, as she was when she walked up to the castle.
Kasimir [weary]: It is a small mercy, though it is more than I gave her.
-> destroyed_close

~ destroyed_yes
Kasimir [sad]: She was never afraid when she was alive, not even of the stones.
Kasimir [weary]: It took three centuries alone to teach her fear, and I left her to learn it.
-> destroyed_close

~ destroyed_unknown
Kasimir [sad]: That is an honest answer, and I will not ask you for a kinder one.
Kasimir [weary]: The dead keep their own counsel at the end.
-> destroyed_close

~ destroyed_close
set kasimir_heard_destroyed
set kasimir_cold
Narrator: Something shutters behind his eyes, quiet and final as the wagon door at his back. He reaches down, takes up the bone needle and the cord, and begins to knot the net again.
Kasimir: Thank you for bringing me the truth of it.
Kasimir: The wind off the lake is rising, and I have work to finish before dark. Good evening to you.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Home, or stay

~ homeward
Kasimir [weary]: My sister always preferred to give the orders, and I find myself inclined, for once, to obey her.
Kasimir [smile]: She told me to go home and be brave where she could not see me.
Kasimir: I would return to the camp by the lake, unless you still have some use for a slow companion.
* Go home, Kasimir, with our thanks. -> homeward_go
* Stay with us a while longer. -> homeward_stay
* We will decide later. Walk with us for now. -> homeward_later

~ homeward_go
set kasimir_homeward_asked
Narrator: He bows with an old-fashioned grace that belongs to a century no one living remembers, then turns toward the road home. He looks lighter than the man who sat mending a net.
Kasimir: Thank you for walking me to the door I could not open alone.
Kasimir [smile]: Walk in the light while it lasts, my friends. If you pass the lake, I will be at the fire, and I will not be mending.
leave kasimir_velikov
-> END

~ homeward_stay
set kasimir_homeward_asked
Kasimir [smile]: She did say to be brave somewhere she could not see me. A road will do.
Kasimir: Very well. I will walk with you a while longer, if only to prove an old elf can learn a new habit.
-> hub_menu

~ homeward_later
Kasimir [weary]: Very well, we will leave the question for another mile. Lead on, and I will keep pace.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The hub

# Opens from the camp's menu and from a click while he walks with the party. When he is travelling after Patrina was
# laid to rest without his asking, the question of going home comes first.
~ talk
if guest:kasimir_velikov and flag.patrina_fate == rest and not flag.kasimir_homeward_asked and not tarokka.ally.npc == kasimir_velikov
-> homeward
endif
if flag.kasimir_cold
-> hub_cold
elif guest:kasimir_velikov and flag.kasimir_bargain == made
-> hub_counting
elif guest:kasimir_velikov
-> hub_road
endif
-> hub_camp

~ hub_camp
Kasimir [smile]: The fire is warm, and the Vistani have been talking. Tell me what you wish to know.
-> hub_menu

~ hub_road
Kasimir: We have a moment before the road takes us again. What is on your mind?
-> hub_menu

~ hub_cold
Kasimir: You have a question for me. Ask it, and let us keep moving.
-> hub_menu

~ hub_counting
Kasimir [weary]: The light is thin today, and my count is smaller. Speak, while we are both here.
-> hub_menu

# The menu shows the three newest topics the party hasn't heard (newest first: a dark gift taken, Vosk, Tarakamedes, the
# Tome, Bluto, the festival, Arabelle), so a visit after a long absence isn't a wall of choices. Each topic is shown
# while it is available and unheard; hearing one makes room for the next. The `kasimir_show_*` flags and
# `kasimir_slots` are only this menu's scratch.
~ hub_menu
set kasimir_slots = 0
set kasimir_show_gift = false
set kasimir_show_broker = false
set kasimir_show_dragon = false
set kasimir_show_tome = false
set kasimir_show_bluto = false
set kasimir_show_festival = false
set kasimir_show_arabelle = false
if flag.kasimir_slots < 3 and flag.dark_gifts_taken >= 1 and not flag.kasimir_heard_gift
set kasimir_show_gift
set kasimir_slots += 1
endif
if flag.kasimir_slots < 3 and flag.kasimir_sister_told and (level >= 8 or visited:tsolenka_pass or guest:kasimir_velikov) and not flag.kasimir_heard_broker
set kasimir_show_broker
set kasimir_slots += 1
endif
if flag.kasimir_slots < 3 and flag.kasimir_sister_told and (level >= 8 or visited:tsolenka_pass or guest:kasimir_velikov) and not flag.kasimir_bargain == made and not flag.kasimir_heard_dragon
set kasimir_show_dragon
set kasimir_slots += 1
endif
if flag.kasimir_slots < 3 and item:tome_of_strahd and not flag.kasimir_heard_tome
set kasimir_show_tome
set kasimir_slots += 1
endif
if flag.kasimir_slots < 3 and flag.bluto_fate and not guest:kasimir_velikov and not flag.kasimir_heard_bluto
set kasimir_show_bluto
set kasimir_slots += 1
endif
if flag.kasimir_slots < 3 and flag.vallaki_backed and not guest:kasimir_velikov and not flag.kasimir_heard_festival
set kasimir_show_festival
set kasimir_slots += 1
endif
if flag.kasimir_slots < 3 and (flag.arabelle_rescued or flag.arabelle_lost) and not guest:kasimir_velikov and not flag.kasimir_heard_arabelle
set kasimir_show_arabelle
set kasimir_slots += 1
endif
if flag.kasimir_slots == 0
Kasimir [weary]: I have no new words for you today. Walk a little further, and perhaps the valley will give us some.
endif
* [if flag.kasimir_show_gift] Tell us what a dark gift costs. -> t_gift
* [if flag.kasimir_show_broker] Tell us about the scholar in the temple. -> t_broker
* [if flag.kasimir_show_dragon] Tell us about the dragon in the red amber. -> t_dragon
* [if flag.kasimir_show_tome] Read the dusk elves' pages in the Tome for us. -> t_tome
* [if flag.kasimir_show_bluto] Tell us what became of Bluto. -> t_bluto
* [if flag.kasimir_show_festival] What is the camp saying about the festival? -> t_festival
* [if flag.kasimir_show_arabelle] Have we heard any word of Arabelle? -> t_arabelle
* [if guest:kasimir_velikov] That is all we need for now. -> END
* [if not guest:kasimir_velikov] Let us talk of something else. -> vallaki/kasimir:menu

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Topics

~ t_festival
set kasimir_heard_festival
if flag.vallaki_backed == baron
-> t_festival_baron
elif flag.vallaki_backed == wachter
-> t_festival_wachter
endif
-> t_festival_neither

~ t_festival_baron
Kasimir: The Vistani say Baron Vargas still sits in his chair in Vallaki. Another festival, and nothing changed.
Kasimir [weary]: A man who orders his people to smile has never understood how long a winter lasts.
-> hub_menu

~ t_festival_wachter
Kasimir: Word from the wagons is that Lady Fiona rules Vallaki now. She has always kept the count's portrait polished.
Kasimir [sad]: The town traded a loud jailer for a quiet clerk of the castle. The doors will lock the same way.
-> hub_menu

~ t_festival_neither
Kasimir: The traders say a council sits in Vallaki now, and the Baron's chair is empty. That is a rare thing here.
Kasimir [weary]: Committees move slowly, which is usually a fault. In this valley, slowness is sometimes a mercy.
-> hub_menu

~ t_arabelle
set kasimir_heard_arabelle
if flag.arabelle_rescued
-> t_arabelle_rescued
endif
-> t_arabelle_lost

~ t_arabelle_rescued
Kasimir [smile]: You brought Luvash his daughter back from the water. Listen to the wagons tonight - the camp has not sung like that in years.
Kasimir: The Vistani remember every hand that pulls a child of theirs from the cold.
-> hub_menu

~ t_arabelle_lost
Kasimir [sad]: The lake kept Luvash's small girl. The fires are low tonight, and her father has not spoken a word since noon.
Kasimir [weary]: I know the sound of a camp when a child does not come home. It takes a long time to fade.
-> hub_menu

~ t_bluto
set kasimir_heard_bluto
if flag.bluto_fate == vistani
-> t_bluto_vistani
elif flag.bluto_fate == killed or flag.bluto_fate == drowned
-> t_bluto_dead
endif
-> t_bluto_lives

~ t_bluto_vistani
Kasimir: You brought the fisherman Bluto to Luvash's people for judgment. I walked down to the water before the camp decided.
Kasimir [weary]: I have seen enough justice in my life. I had no need to watch another man's.
-> hub_menu

~ t_bluto_dead
Kasimir: They say the fisherman Bluto is dead by Lake Zarovich. A sack, a boat, and a short end to a small madness.
Kasimir [sad]: It does not dry the water, of course. It only leaves one fewer fisherman on the shore.
-> hub_menu

~ t_bluto_lives
Kasimir: I heard that Bluto still breathes after what he did at the lake. You left him his life.
Kasimir [weary]: Living with one's own hands is a long punishment. Believe me, I know the measure of it.
-> hub_menu

~ t_tome
set kasimir_heard_tome
Narrator: He lifts the leather cover with slow, steady fingers, as though one rough breath might turn the old paper to ash.
Kasimir [weary]: So this is Strahd's own hand. A conqueror bored by peace, a brother named Sergei, and a girl named Tatyana who chose the fall.
Kasimir: Look here - one dry page for the dusk elves, written the way a landlord notes his tenants. Not a word more.
Kasimir [sad]: One of ours stayed in that house to serve him, yet even we are only a footnote in the ledger.
Kasimir [sad]: I looked for Patrina's name in the margins. He did not even write her down.
-> hub_menu

~ t_gift
set kasimir_heard_gift
Narrator: His dark eyes rest on your hands for a heartbeat too long, reading the new stillness under your skin.
Kasimir [sad]: You took a gift from the amber. I can see it in the way your breath catches, and how you do not flinch.
Kasimir: The wardens carved their warnings plainly, because the vestiges always keep their word. A permanent grace, for a permanent debt.
Kasimir [weary]: I will not judge you for buying what you needed. Only remember that the bill is collected at the end.
-> hub_menu

~ t_dragon
set kasimir_heard_dragon
if flag.vestige_tarakamedes_heard
if flag.kasimir_bargain == refused
-> t_dragon_refused
endif
-> t_dragon_after
endif
-> t_dragon_before

~ t_dragon_before
Kasimir: In the red amber lies Tarakamedes, the dragon in the grave. The old books say it deals in the dead.
Kasimir [weary]: I have read the name for three hundred years, though never the price it asks.
Kasimir [sad]: Do not trust me when we stand before that stone. If I speak to it, do not take my word on the day.
-> hub_menu

~ t_dragon_after
Kasimir [weary]: So Tarakamedes has spoken to you out of the red amber. Do not tell me what it said.
Kasimir [sad]: I am glad you were the ones to hear that voice, and that I did not stand before it alone.
-> hub_menu

~ t_dragon_refused
Kasimir [sad]: My hand was on the red amber, and you pulled me back from my own word.
Kasimir [weary]: Thank you for the mercy, though it sits like a stone in my chest.
-> hub_menu

~ t_broker
set kasimir_heard_broker
if flag.vosk_met
-> t_broker_after
endif
-> t_broker_before

~ t_broker_before
Kasimir: Rumour speaks of a Master Vosk in the halls - a scholar of the temple who keeps its accounts.
Kasimir: They say he is courteous, glad of visitors, and very helpful to those who lose their way in the cold.
Kasimir [weary]: Read old books long enough and you learn one rule. In a market like that, the politest voice is the one with a price list.
-> hub_menu

~ t_broker_after
Kasimir [weary]: You have met Master Vosk, then, and heard a clerk's courtesy in the ice.
Kasimir: Men who keep neat ledgers in ruins never lack for ink.
-> hub_menu
